## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
1. Run `.\mvnw clean compile` to verify clean compilation with zero warnings/errors.
2. Run `.\mvnw test` to verify context loading.

### Manual / Integration Verification
1. Launch the application: `.\mvnw spring-boot:run`.
2. Test HTTP endpoints via PowerShell `Invoke-RestMethod` / `curl`:
   - `GET /api/hello` -> Verify 200 OK response `{"message": "Hello World REST API"}`.
   - `POST /api/employees` -> Verify 201 Created response and JSON payload for valid employee.
   - `POST /api/employees` (duplicate email/mobile) -> Verify 409 Conflict error.
   - `POST /api/employees` (invalid email/blank name) -> Verify 400 Bad Request with validation errors.
   - `GET /api/employees` -> Verify 200 OK returning list of employees.
   - `GET /api/employees/1` -> Verify 200 OK returning employee details.
   - `GET /api/employees/999` -> Verify 404 Not Found error response.
   - `PUT /api/employees/1` -> Verify 200 OK returning updated employee details.
   - `DELETE /api/employees/1` -> Verify 204 No Content response.
   - `GET /api/employees/1` after delete -> Verify 404 Not Found.
